      "created_at": "2019-07-21T23:22:10Z",
      "updated_at": "2019-07-21T23:22:10Z",
      "body": "The web [push-api](https://w3c.github.io/push-api/) subscription includes [an encryption key](https://w3c.github.io/push-api/#pushencryptionkeyname-enumeration) so that the push notification payload is not visible to the gateway. I'd love to see synapse implement a push gateway which supports the web push-api.\r\n\r\nI think the same technique could be used for sending the notifications to APNS or GCM and then on the client side it would decrypt the message before displaying the notification. If so, this could potentially save a lot of battery over waking up the radio again when the push message is handled to fetch the payload.",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
      "reactions": {
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/matrix-org/synapse/issues/comments/513596299/reactions",
