      "created_at": "2021-10-20T14:49:51Z",
      "updated_at": "2021-10-20T14:51:58Z",
      "body": "So it seems that all a client needs to do to not leak message contents is to use the [`event_id_only` format](https://spec.matrix.org/unstable/client-server-api/#post_matrixclientv3pushersset) when setting up a pusher. The Element clients already do this.\r\n\r\nIn addition to this, Synapse implements the `include_content` setting referred to in the screenshot above. Setting this to `false` makes Synapse withhold the content even if *not* using `event_id_only`. We currently default to `true` here. Could we change the default to `false` for good measure? (It's been suggested this might require a spec change, but I don't think this is the case as the Push Gateway API says the `content` field may be withheld for any reason)\r\n\r\nOther than potentially changing that default, I don't think there's anything else left to do here.",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "pin": null,
      "reactions": {
